        a                              ecrm:E22_Man-Made_Object ;
        rdfs:comment                   "A sash of crimson plyed silk yarn, worked in the sprang technique, probably with a circular warp, with a fringe at each end.  It is worked in a pattern of diamonds and horizontal bands with a crown, inscription and date at each end."@en , "Military sash of crimson silk sprang, English, 1773, \"GR THE 3\" with crown"@en ;
